      "Language": "eng",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "On the base of a wide clinical experiences, the Authors report some consideration about relationship between clinical findings and neuroradiological pictures (plain film, myelography, CT and NMR) of the lumbar vertebral and disc diseases. It's pointed out the useful aspect of each imaging technique that contribute to obtain the more complete informations about anatomy of the lesion; such considerations allows the surgeon to plain the more adequate surgical technique. The Authors think myelography, still today, is the investigation of choice in this kind of pathology."},
